00:18:20.534 --> 00:18:23.234
-Did you at least feel
that they had, um...

00:18:23.234 --> 00:18:26.267
used the spirit of the song
correctly?

00:18:26.267 --> 00:18:29.000
[ Laughter ]

00:18:29.000 --> 00:18:30.667
-That's a loaded question.

00:18:30.667 --> 00:18:32.200
[ Laughter ]

00:18:32.200 --> 00:18:33.767
-Wow.
-Well, now, what was the title?

00:18:33.767 --> 00:18:34.901
What was the title of the song?

00:18:34.901 --> 00:18:36.868
-They probably did use
the song correctly

00:18:36.868 --> 00:18:39.968
'cause it was called
"Just Another One Night Stand."

00:18:39.968 --> 00:18:41.567
-All right. Well...

00:18:41.567 --> 00:18:42.901
-Yeah.
-Yeah, they tend not --

00:18:42.901 --> 00:18:45.367
Those films don't tend to have
the longer relationship.

00:18:45.367 --> 00:18:49.367
-It involved -- It involved a...

00:18:49.367 --> 00:18:53.033
young woman wearing
a cowboy hat and cowboy boots,

00:18:53.033 --> 00:18:56.367
a gas station,
and a couple of cowboys.

00:18:56.367 --> 00:18:58.534
-Yeah.
-And a pickup truck.

00:18:58.534 --> 00:19:00.767
-[ Laughs ]

00:19:00.767 --> 00:19:02.267
-That's all we're going to say.

00:19:02.267 --> 00:19:04.334
We don't need to keep
talking about it.

00:19:04.334 --> 00:19:06.567
-If you've seen
one of them ever,

00:19:06.567 --> 00:19:08.968
you can probably finish it.
-Pretty much. Yes.

00:19:08.968 --> 00:19:10.934
Well, I'll tell you
the name of it.

00:19:10.934 --> 00:19:11.934
-The name of the movie?

00:19:11.934 --> 00:19:13.567
-Yes.
-Okay.

00:19:13.567 --> 00:19:17.634
-It was called...
[ Laughter ]

00:19:17.634 --> 00:19:20.834
You're making me laugh.

00:19:20.834 --> 00:19:23.634
It was called
"All-American Girls in Heat."

00:19:23.634 --> 00:19:25.033
-Oh.
-"Part Two."

00:19:25.033 --> 00:19:26.300
-"Part Two"?
-"Part Two." Yeah.

00:19:26.300 --> 00:19:28.000
-Well, that's good.

00:19:28.000 --> 00:19:31.300
I mean, and do you think --
Do you think, for people

00:19:31.300 --> 00:19:33.467
that are looking it up,
they should see the first one?

00:19:33.467 --> 00:19:35.567
Do you think
they'll be able to follow

00:19:35.567 --> 00:19:37.701
the plot of the second one
if they haven't...?

00:19:37.701 --> 00:19:39.133
-Yeah, I think they'll be able
to pick up

00:19:39.133 --> 00:19:42.367
right where
the other one left off.

00:19:42.367 --> 00:19:44.033
-So, you worked
with Adam before.

00:19:44.033 --> 00:19:45.701
You also worked with Fred.

00:19:45.701 --> 00:19:47.868
-Oh.
-And -- Okay.

00:19:47.868 --> 00:19:49.067
But this is a true --

00:19:49.067 --> 00:19:51.901
Fred used to open for Wilco
doing stand-up.

00:19:51.901 --> 00:19:53.367
-Yeah, I didn't know
he was gonna be here.

00:19:53.367 --> 00:19:54.667
-Oh, okay.

00:19:54.667 --> 00:19:58.400
Was it a weird vibe
back in the day?

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:00.133
-He owes my wife a lot of money.

00:20:00.133 --> 00:20:01.400
-Oh, yeah.

00:20:01.400 --> 00:20:03.667
So this is a --
You --

00:20:03.667 --> 00:20:05.000
[ Laughter ]

00:20:05.000 --> 00:20:08.801
This is true that Fred
made a promise to your wife.

00:20:08.801 --> 00:20:11.400
-He made a legal document.

00:20:11.400 --> 00:20:14.100
-Okay.
-Several times, we -- Yeah.

00:20:14.100 --> 00:20:17.567
-And, now, what was the impetus
of Fred making this --

00:20:17.567 --> 00:20:20.567
-My wife gave him his start
in show business

00:20:20.567 --> 00:20:22.367
by allowing him
to answer the phones

00:20:22.367 --> 00:20:23.734
at the rock club that she owned.

00:20:23.734 --> 00:20:25.467
-Okay. This is true, Fred?
-Sure.

00:20:25.467 --> 00:20:29.634
-Okay, and so in return,
what did Fred promise your wife?

00:20:29.634 --> 00:20:32.634
-Initially, he promised 50%
of all of his earnings.

00:20:32.634 --> 00:20:35.400
-Okay.
[ Laughter ]

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:38.334
-And then when she
confronted him about it...

00:20:38.334 --> 00:20:40.100
-Sure, as you would
if he didn't pay up.

00:20:40.100 --> 00:20:42.801
-...he said he was sorry

00:20:42.801 --> 00:20:46.267
and he would give her 75%.
-Got it.

00:20:46.267 --> 00:20:48.634
And, now, you've actually
brought the legal document?

00:20:48.634 --> 00:20:49.767
-I do have the document with me.

00:20:49.767 --> 00:20:51.834
-Now, it is a video document.
-Yes.

00:20:51.834 --> 00:20:53.434
-And, Fred, you will confirm
that you made this?

00:20:53.434 --> 00:20:55.133
-Yes.
-Okay. Here is Fred.

00:20:55.133 --> 00:20:59.634
And hopefully, if anybody here,
you know, passed the bar --

00:20:59.634 --> 00:21:02.200
-I have my lawyer with me.
-Okay, great. Alright.

00:21:02.200 --> 00:21:04.868
Let's see if you believe
this is a legal document.

00:21:04.868 --> 00:21:07.067
-This is a legal document
without jokes,

00:21:07.067 --> 00:21:09.133
without irony or sarcasm.

00:21:09.133 --> 00:21:10.767
This is not an exaggeration.

00:21:10.767 --> 00:21:13.968
I, from now on,

00:21:13.968 --> 00:21:17.133
owe Susan Miller

00:21:17.133 --> 00:21:19.200
75% of my income.

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:20.300
It used to be 50%.

00:21:20.300 --> 00:21:22.367
It's up to 75%
because retroactively

00:21:22.367 --> 00:21:24.467
going back to the amount
I owe her before,

00:21:24.467 --> 00:21:26.334
I need to add to that.

00:21:26.334 --> 00:21:30.601
That is all monies brought in by
any comedy or any entertainment.

00:21:30.601 --> 00:21:31.701
That is what's owed.

00:21:31.701 --> 00:21:33.734
If you are a lawyer
looking at this,

00:21:33.734 --> 00:21:36.734
there is no irony in my face
or, like, any winking.

00:21:36.734 --> 00:21:38.367
I owe this money.

00:21:38.367 --> 00:21:40.133
By the way, immediately.

00:21:40.133 --> 00:21:41.734
[ Laughter ]

00:21:41.734 --> 00:21:43.701
-I mean, I think
that's a legal document.

00:21:43.701 --> 00:21:45.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:21:45.934 --> 00:21:47.901
-I -- Slam dunk.

00:21:47.901 --> 00:21:49.367
-But Fred's
a little shady, though.

00:21:49.367 --> 00:21:51.200
That's the problem.
Is it true that when Fred --

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:53.300
-How much could it be?

00:21:53.300 --> 00:21:55.100
-How much could it be?
-10 grand?

00:21:55.100 --> 00:21:56.667
-10 grand?
-Something in there, yeah.

00:21:56.667 --> 00:21:57.868
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:21:57.868 --> 00:22:00.567
-You've made probably around
12 to 15 grand.

00:22:00.567 --> 00:22:02.300
-I would say 12 to 15.
-Yeah.

00:22:02.300 --> 00:22:04.000
So then you're getting
75% of that.

00:22:04.000 --> 00:22:05.434
You're gonna do pretty well.

00:22:05.434 --> 00:22:08.267
You did something on the show
that I get --

00:22:08.267 --> 00:22:11.400
I will be honest -- you --
you -- you threw your shoe.

00:22:11.400 --> 00:22:12.701
This is a photo of you.

00:22:12.701 --> 00:22:14.100
Someone was singing.
They finished their song.

00:22:14.100 --> 00:22:15.667
I believe it was
"Try a Little Tenderness."

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:16.868
Was that the song?
-Yes.

00:22:16.868 --> 00:22:18.868
-Which is --
was incredibly well sung.

00:22:18.868 --> 00:22:21.434
And then you threw your shoe,
which -- I will be honest --

00:22:21.434 --> 00:22:23.234
if I was onstage
and a shoe came up...

00:22:23.234 --> 00:22:24.400
[ Laughter ]

00:22:24.400 --> 00:22:26.567
...I'd think that was
an unsatisfied customer.

00:22:26.567 --> 00:22:27.834
-No!
-Okay, interesting.

00:22:27.834 --> 00:22:29.701
-It is a compliment.
-It is a compliment.

00:22:29.701 --> 00:22:31.934
-Well, at J-Hud Productions,
it's a compliment.

00:22:31.934 --> 00:22:33.734
-Gotcha.
-Come on, now.

00:22:33.734 --> 00:22:35.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:22:35.868 --> 00:22:37.267
If you move me enough

00:22:37.267 --> 00:22:39.667
that I remove my shoe
to throw it at you,

00:22:39.667 --> 00:22:41.734
you have done something
just amazing.

00:22:41.734 --> 00:22:42.934
-That's fanta--

00:22:42.934 --> 00:22:44.267
-Like, it's equivalent
to a standing ovation.

00:22:44.267 --> 00:22:45.367
-Interesting.
-Yeah.

00:22:45.367 --> 00:22:46.601
-Has this been your --

00:22:46.601 --> 00:22:48.067
Has anyone
ever thrown a shoe at you?

00:22:48.067 --> 00:22:49.501
-Oh, yes.
-Okay.

00:22:49.501 --> 00:22:53.133
-I did -- I had an audition
for a tour with Barry Manilow,

00:22:53.133 --> 00:22:55.400
like, I don't know
how many years ago that was.

00:22:55.400 --> 00:22:56.767
And I sang a song.

00:22:56.767 --> 00:22:58.934
And the people who
I was auditioning in front of --

00:22:58.934 --> 00:23:00.934
they literally threw everything
at me off of the desk.

00:23:00.934 --> 00:23:02.234
-Wow!
[ Light laughter ]

00:23:02.234 --> 00:23:03.734
-And I was just standing there
like, "Oh, my God."

00:23:03.734 --> 00:23:05.901
It was shoes. It was notebooks.
It was pens and everything.

00:23:05.901 --> 00:23:07.834
They was like,
"Girl, you better sing!"

00:23:07.834 --> 00:23:09.033
[ Laughter ]
-That's great.

00:23:09.033 --> 00:23:11.000
-So when somebody's singing
for me...

00:23:11.000 --> 00:23:12.133
-You get -- yeah.
-...you might catch a shoe.

00:23:12.133 --> 00:23:13.567
And if I could get this boot off
right now...

00:23:13.567 --> 00:23:14.567
-Yeah, well, that's --
[ Laughter ]

00:23:14.567 --> 00:23:15.834
Now, this is interesting,

00:23:15.834 --> 00:23:17.200
